OHIRA-0008

REST API & Integration Specification

Project: Ohira

Document ID: OHIRA-0008

Version: 1.0

Status: Founder's Draft


---

Purpose

The Ohira REST API exposes project intelligence to external systems.

Rather than forcing applications to understand a project's source code, they consume structured knowledge through stable HTTP endpoints.

Consumers include:

Web applications

Mobile applications

VS Code Extension

JetBrains Plugin

GitHub App

MCP Server

AI Assistants

CI/CD Pipelines

Smart Property

Future third-party integrations



---

API Design Principles

Resource-Oriented

Every endpoint represents a resource.

Examples:

/projects
/analysis
/plugins
/context
/reports


---

Versioned

Every public API is versioned.

/api/v1

Future:

/api/v2

Breaking changes must never affect existing clients.


---

JSON First

All endpoints return JSON by default.

Future support:

YAML

Markdown

NDJSON (streaming)



---

Stateless

Every request contains all required information.

The server should never rely on in-memory client state.


